# Two Federation destroyers on layouts/nebula.jsonc get the same move order along +X: Inside starts in a row of Mutara
# nebulae and Outside in clear space. The dump (3 s) shows Inside's speed (vel=) below Outside's while Inside is in
# the row. The path planner costs the row at the nebulae's pathing_cost of 400 (against the default 100) over their
# effect radius times 1.8, so Inside's path leaves the row by a bend: its velocity there points off +X, where Outside's
# stays on +X.
# Run it with --layout layouts/nebula.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 0.3
select Inside
move 2400 -2000
wait 0.1
select Outside
move 2400 -2300
wait 3
dump inside
